{"id":"int-ae07f165","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-06-29T22:44:01.35191777Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-ysji.4","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Added 'fact' metric kind (single + ratio over FactTables): schema (FactMetricCreate + FactOperand), service validation (fact-table existence/project ownership, measure/distinct membership in fact_table.columns + validate_identifier, row_filter as a stored-filter name, per-aggregation rules), collection (_collect_fact single/ratio reusing adapter get_time_bucketed_aggregate(+breakdown) + evaluate_composition divide-by-zero->gap), value-kind (count/count_distinct count-shaped, sum/avg/min/max + ratio fractional). FULLY removed legacy fact_aggregation: enum value (PG type-recreation migration b3c4d5e6f7a8, single head, pre-flight DELETE makes USING cast safe, restartable via DROP TYPE IF EXISTS), schemas, collector, all docstrings, FE surface. Hardened: row-filter fragments now block SELECT/WITH subqueries; runtime fact-table project-scope check; empty-columns guard; asserts->raises; idempotent migration. Gates: ruff/mypy clean, 221 backend tests + contract + alembic-single-head, FE tsc/eslint/vitest green. 1 HIGH (ratio adapter leak) + 5 MEDIUM + selected LOW all fixed."}}
{"id":"int-ec0614e7","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-06-29T23:19:35.727483349Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-ysji.5","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Frontend complete: FactTables page (list + create/edit with SQL editor, 'Preview columns' via /preview populating persisted columns, named row-filters editor) + factTablesApi + types + routes + 'Fact tables' nav item + breadcrumb. Rewrote the metric 'fact' form: fact-table picker -> column/aggregation/filter dropdowns, single + ratio (numerator/denominator, possibly different fact tables), client validation mirroring backend rules. Gates: tsc/eslint clean, 22 vitest tests. 4 HIGH (a11y labels, double tab stop, stale-edit key, unsafe agg cast) + 5 MEDIUM (stable row-filter keys, aria-required, query-key casing, dead guard, exhaustive kind dispatch) all fixed."}}
{"id":"int-9a4989c8","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-06-29T23:19:38.884856532Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-ysji","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Epic complete (6/6 slices). Replaced legacy fact_aggregation with a fact-table model: FactTables defined separately (SQL SELECT + introspected columns + timestamp + named row filters); fact metrics built point-and-click on top (column + aggregation + filter), single + ratio. Shipped backend (model/migration, introspection, CRUD/preview, fact kind collection + ratio, full fact_aggregation removal via enum-recreation migration b3c4d5e6f7a8) and frontend (FactTables page + rich fact form + nav). All waves committed on feat/metrics-catalog; gates green throughout. Follow-up: tripl- demo-data seeding of metrics + fact tables."}}
{"id":"int-077bd76a","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-06-29T23:31:13.175336208Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-saur","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Extended create_demo_project (demo_service.py section 14) to seed the metrics catalog: an 'orders' FactTable (read-only SELECT + 6 introspected columns + a named 'completed' row filter), and 4 MetricDefinitions covering every kind — a sql metric (Active Sessions), an event_composition ratio (Purchase conversion = purchases/home views), a fact single (Revenue completed = sum(amount) filtered), and a fact ratio (Average order value = sum/count). Definitions built via the Pydantic create schemas (to_create_values) so validators run and config is exact, persisted as ORM rows to keep the seeder's single commit. Pre-collected MetricValue series fabricated (7d hourly for the ratio on the scan grid; 30d daily for sql/fact) so the catalog + drilldowns render with data. 2 new demo tests assert the catalog + fact table render via the API. Gates: ruff/mypy clean, 8 demo tests pass."}}
{"id":"int-26f03f8c","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-06-30T07:17:13.384500173Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-tj7x","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Not reproducible — transient stale-cache artifact, not a code bug. Verified after a clean reload: GET /api/v1/data-sources returns all sources (incl. the project's own), the fact-table edit form preselects the saved data_source_id correctly, and the fact-tables list resolves the data source name. Original observation was caused by a stale shared React Query ['data-sources'] cache (old browser tab from before the stack rebuild) plus creating the demo via a raw in-page fetch that bypassed query invalidation. Both forms use the identical query (queryKey ['data-sources'], dataSourcesApi.list()); no divergence in code."}}
{"id":"int-9f1f2a75","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-06-30T08:52:32.651552672Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-tdsi","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Batched fact-metric collection shipped. Adapter contract (base.py AggregateSpec + get_time_bucketed_multi_aggregate/_breakdown) implemented in ClickHouse/Postgres/BigQuery with conditional aggregates (sumIf/countIf/-If vs FILTER (WHERE)/CASE); empty conditional groups guarded to NULL (count sentinel / NULLIF) so values stay identical to the per-metric path. Batched collector + collect_fact_metrics_batch task: dedup specs per fact table, covering window chunked by smallest replay_chunk_interval (disjoint-bucket merge), one multi-aggregate query per fact table + one per breakdown dimension, single/same-table/cross-table ratio assembled via evaluate_composition, per-metric upsert + error isolation. Scheduler groups due fact metrics by interval -> one batch dispatch; sql/event_composition unchanged; per-metric _collect_fact kept as fallback. Gates: ruff/mypy clean, full suite 915 passed; 1 CRITICAL + 3 HIGH review findings (ClickHouse avgIf/minIf/maxIf NaN/extremes, 0-vs-NULL across dialects, replay_chunk_interval ignored) all fixed."}}
