{"id":"int-7d5fcbba","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-11T15:34:59.552052112Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.2","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Split monolithic seeder into versioned demo/ scenario package: scenario.py (DemoContext + DemoScenario recipe + non-committing orchestrator), noise.py (deterministic hashlib-based derive_seed replacing salted builtin hash), builders/{plan,variables,activity,warehouse,monitoring,catalog,branches,search}.py. Preserves real detect_anomalies + compute_psi. New API-visible examples: event meta values, event-type relation, event-type owner (creator only, never invented), authored per-event variable override, event change history, figma photo (external_url, no stored bytes), feature-branch journey (revision+branch+comment). Validated *Create schemas retained for fact/metrics. DEMO_RECIPE_VERSION 1->2. OpenAPI unchanged. 23 targeted tests green (incl. new test_demo_scenario.py: determinism + per-example visibility + isolated builder). Full suite/E2E deferred to tripl-2su6.10."}}
{"id":"int-5825798d","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-11T16:13:48.327139525Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.3","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"SyntheticAdapter (core/adapters/synthetic.py): bounded deterministic in-memory events+orders dataset (hashlib seed, no network/filesystem), implements the full BaseAdapter contract by aggregating rows from structured params (time windows, breakdowns, top-N/Other, multi-aggregate, agg fns), matching ClickHouse row layouts. New db_type 'synthetic' (DBType enum + migration e3f4a5b6c7d8 ALTER TYPE ADD VALUE); registered in registry. Unsupported SQL raises SyntheticCapabilityError (never fabricates). SQL metric active_sessions shape supported. Demo warehouse builder now uses db_type=synthetic (no demo.internal host). Guards: create rejects synthetic; update locks host/port/db/user/password/type; real<->synthetic conversion blocked; scan_service._verify_data_source rejects cross-project synthetic selection (ordinary project 422); synthetic excluded from DB_TYPE_OPTIONS. is_synthetic label on DataSourceResponse; OpenAPI+frontend types regenerated. Production adapters untouched. Tests: test_synthetic_adapter.py (24 contract), TestSyntheticGuards, scan-config guard test; 75+38 targeted green. Frontend test-mock touchups for is_synthetic deferred to .10."}}
{"id":"int-82e0bc8a","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-11T18:36:49.646858138Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.4","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Demo scan surface + governance over the synthetic source. ScanConfig now scan-ready (event_type_column=event_type groups synthetic rows into authored types; platform_column, app_version_column, replay_chunk_interval) so Preview/Run now/Replay/scheduled run the real pipeline over SyntheticAdapter with no network. New demo/builders/governance.py (wired after monitoring): ScanJob history (3 completed + 1 old safely-explained failure; created_at=run-time so latest job is completed and project summary reads healthy, failing_scan_config_count=0), CoverageMetric reconciling with per-type scanned volume (matched<=total, ~94%), 2 ShadowEventCandidate with names OUTSIDE the plan (no source-identity collision), one age-valid dead event. Live-pipeline proof: registry.build_adapter over the demo synthetic source returns real preview rows (event_type in {screen_view,click,purchase}) with no host contacted. Tests: test_demo_scans.py (6); full demo suite 31 green; OpenAPI unchanged. DEFERRED to tripl-2su6.10: full Celery worker-transition E2E (Run now/Replay endpoint -> job pending->running->completed) — blocked by the async(request)/sync(worker) in-memory-DB test split; the warehouse-facing data path is proven at the adapter boundary here."}}
{"id":"int-637f2f92","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-11T19:13:43.364827864Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.5","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Demo catalog metrics now backed by the synthetic dataset + real collectors. Worker-integration test (test_demo_metric_collection.py, 6): real collect_metric_definitions over the REAL SyntheticAdapter on a sync DB — sql/fact-single/fact-ratio/event_composition all collect real MetricValue with last_collection_status=success+last_collected_at; a country-breakdown fact metric produces real MetricValueBreakdown; collect_fact_metrics_batch groups revenue+AOV into ONE shared orders scan (call-count asserted); window re-collect is idempotent (no dup rows); an unsupported metric_sql records status=error with a safe message and writes NO values; real detect_anomalies flags an injected spike over the collected series. Fact-table preview + schema refresh serve synthetic orders through the normal API (introspect_fact_table -> build_adapter -> SyntheticAdapter); new API test. Catalog builder no longer fabricates sinusoids: revenue (filtered daily SUM via multi-aggregate), AOV (SUM/COUNT one scan), active_sessions (sql get_preview_rows path) are adapter-derived from the synthetic rows; conversion stays a real 0-1 fraction from EventMetric. One minimal synthetic-adapter fix: paren-aware row-filter evaluator for batched conditional aggregates (still raises capability error for non-grouping parens); 24 adapter tests green, production adapters/collectors untouched, OpenAPI unchanged. 48 targeted green. KNOWN GAP: single-metric fact path get_time_bucketed_aggregate ignores WHERE filter on the synthetic adapter (batched path applies it); demo derives revenue via the filtered path. DEFERRED to .10: in-provisioning real worker dispatch + scheduled next-bucket beat->collect E2E (async-request/sync-worker harness split)."}}
{"id":"int-93106909","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-11T20:00:31.838159312Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.6","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"No-network demo alert sink. New AlertDestinationType.demo_sink (migration f1a2b3c4d5e8 ALTER TYPE ADD VALUE) — a local, credential-free sink. send_alert_delivery has an elif demo_sink branch that renders via _render_delivery_message and records the message into AlertDelivery/AlertDeliveryItem with local markers (delivery_mode=local_sink, is_local, simulated) and makes ZERO network calls; else: raise preserved; production slack/telegram/webhook/email/jira/linear senders and alerts_channels.py UNCHANGED. Guards (_alerting_destinations): demo_sink create only on Project.is_demo (422 else); demo_sink cannot be given real credentials on update; type immutable so real<->demo_sink conversion impossible; no secrets stored. demo/builders/alerts.py (scenario after catalog, DEMO_RECIPE_VERSION 2->3): a demo_sink destination + a visibly-disabled slack example (no creds), a FIRING rule covering all anomaly scopes (project/event-type/event/metric) + schema/distribution/variable-value/release-regression opt-ins driven by the real seeded anomalies, a healthy rule, AlertRuleState (firing+healthy), one locally-rendered AlertDelivery+items, AlertCorrelationState inbox group, and a ChartAnnotation explaining the injected spike. Simulate is render-only; retry re-enqueues to the same local branch. API labels is_local/is_simulated on destination+delivery responses; OpenAPI + frontend types regenerated; demo_sink kept OUT of user-selectable create options. NETWORK-DENY TEST (test_demo_alert_sink.py): socket/httpx/smtplib patched to raise; create+dispatch+simulate+retry of demo_sink all succeed with zero outbound calls. 82 targeted green (incl. full test_alerting.py, production unchanged). Frontend badge display + is_synthetic/is_local mock touchups deferred to .10."}}
{"id":"int-b04d6bf5","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-11T20:44:33.261903393Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.7","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Demo runtime tick keeps active demos fresh. Project.demo_last_tick_at + demo_last_accessed_at (migration f2a3b4c5d6e7). Feature flag settings.demo_runtime_enabled (off => no-op, real scheduling untouched). Cadence = real catch-up: worker/tasks/demo_runtime.py::advance_demos (beat every 300s) appends hourly buckets from the demo's last populated bucket to newest complete hour. Selector: is_demo AND generation_status=ready AND active (demo_last_accessed_at within DEMO_IDLE_PAUSE_MINUTES=6h, else paused/skipped). Per-project pg_advisory_xact_lock (no-op off Postgres). Deterministic append via demo/noise.py derive_seed/hourly_volume/platform_shares anchored to demo_seeded_at (shape-identical to seed, no spike re-inject): per-event+per-type EventMetric, EventMetricBreakdown, CoverageMetric, conversion MetricValue. Idempotent: pre-check + begin_nested savepoint swallowing IntegrityError + unique bucket constraints => concurrent/retried ticks converge to one result. New completed ScanJob per tick (real execution, result_summary.demo_runtime_tick). Real detect_anomalies recompute over fresh 48h window (delete-window-then-insert, guarded by ProjectAnomalySettings). Retention prune EventMetric/breakdown/coverage/MetricValue/MetricAnomaly/DistributionDrift/SchemaDrift/ScanJob beyond DEMO_RETENTION_DAYS=23 => capped per-demo growth. Status emit: cache.sync_delete_prefix(projects + signals:slug) for .8. Pause/resume: project_service.get_project bumps demo_last_accessed_at for demos (throttled 60s, commit after serialization to avoid MissingGreenlet; no-op for real projects). No authored plan mutation. Tests test_demo_runtime.py: two ticks stay fresh past 3h horizon, same-clock double-run idempotent, partial-failure-safe, retention cap, pause->skip->resume, flag-off no-op, non-demo untouched. 27 targeted green; API unchanged. FOLLOW-UP for .10: the demo ScanConfig is still eligible for check_metrics_due->collect_metrics (two idempotent writers); reconcile/exclude demos from the real dispatcher in production."}}
{"id":"int-23c9a5f0","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-11T21:52:51.765835917Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.8","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Project-scoped live updates. Backend: GET /projects/{slug}/events/stream (events_stream.py, SSE text/event-stream, include_in_schema=False so OpenAPI unchanged), auth+project-scoped via get_current_user/_enforce_project_scope (anon 401, foreign key 403, wrong slug 404); named events scan_job.updated/metric_collection.updated/activity.created/signals.updated/project_summary.updated; hello event announces redis|degraded; heartbeat + monotonic id + Last-Event-ID reconnect cursor with bounded Redis ring replay; degrades gracefully with Redis off. Bus realtime.py: publish_project_event (sync+async) per-project channel tripl:events:{slug}, INCR seq + capped LPUSH/LTRIM, no-op off Redis; two new cache.py accessors. After-COMMIT publishers wired: scan.py (run_scan transitions + apply_event_groups), metrics/tasks.py (collect_metrics terminal/failure + signals), demo_runtime.py (.7 tick), alerts.py (send_alert_delivery). Frontend realtime/: invalidationMap.ts (event->query-key-prefix, prefix matching so divergent keys reached without rewriting call sites), useProjectEventStream.ts (EventSource + backoff reconnect w/ cursor + monotonic-id dedupe, mounted once in Layout), pollingPolicy.ts (hidden-tab->off, stream live->off, terminal->stop) migrating all 14 refetchInterval sites to adaptive (idle pages poll only when stream down). Tests: backend test_project_event_stream + 163 worker/stream green (publish safe w/ Redis off); frontend lint 0 warnings + 21 new vitest green. DEFERRED to .10: browser E2E (2 clients/reconnect/fallback/navigation). SEPARATE: frontend pnpm build has 8 PRE-EXISTING type-drift errors from .3(synthetic/is_synthetic)/.6(demo_sink) in untouched files — being fixed next as .3/.6 cleanup, then .10 legacy handling."}}
{"id":"int-5302fa02","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-11T22:46:55.047914473Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.9","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Demo provisioning UX + capability-aware product tour (frontend, src/demo/). Provisioning: useDemoProvisioning (blocking POST /projects/demo with ref-based duplicate-request guard, timed phase animation, success->Overview welcome not Events, retry=fresh create) + DemoProvisioningDialog (staged phases, aria-live/role=status a11y, not-dismissible-in-flight, inline 500 error + Try again). Overview welcome panel (DemoWelcomePanel) + ProductTour/tourSteps stepper deep-linking Events/Scans/Live activity/Metrics+Fact tables/Monitors/Anomalies/Coverage/Reconciliation/Branches/Alert preview, with fact tables + 4 metric kinds directly discoverable. Persistent DemoBanner (Layout): local-synthetic badge, recipe version, demo_seeded_at freshness, whats-simulated limits, Reset/Delete via confirm dialog hitting demo-scoped creator/owner endpoints (delete->/workspace). Onboarding real-action gating (onboarding-utils): hasExecutedScanJob (seeded ScanConfig != Run a scan), countRealSources (is_synthetic excluded from Connect a source). Capability labels (capabilityBadges): SyntheticSourceBadge, LocalDeliveryBadge (simulated delivery never shows real send), never conflates synthetic/local vs real/success. Scans loading/error/empty fixed + summarizeScanChanges +N events/metrics/signals chips on completion (via .8 live stream). No API change. 34 new vitest cover pending/success/500/retry/duplicate/navigation, badge reset/delete confirm, onboarding gating, capability badges, tour discoverability. build green, lint 0 warnings, 683/684 tests (1 = pre-existing flaky App redirect that passes isolated). DEFERRED to .10: browser E2E (2 clients, live tour without refresh, reconnect)."}}
{"id":"int-3796dab2","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-11T23:50:34.172884534Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.10","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Epic close-out. Legacy handling: demo_legacy_service classifies real|legacy|outdated|current-demo from a STRICT CONJUNCTION (legacy source name LIKE 'Demo warehouse %' AND host demo.internal AND clickhouse) referenced/owned by a non-is_demo project — a demo-* slug/name alone is NEVER a marker (negative tests). ProjectResponse.demo_legacy/demo_outdated wired in _serialize_project + batched list. POST /projects/demo/{slug}/upgrade re-provisions legacy(adopt+reset+orphan-sweep)/outdated demos in place; refuses to overwrite an EDITED demo (Event.updated_at>seed anchor) unless force=true (fixed a real crash: heuristic used Variable.updated_at which doesn't exist). cleanup_orphan_legacy_sources removes ONLY unowned+unreferenced legacy sources. Rollback: settings.demo_enabled gates ONLY provisioning (403), never real projects (test). Telemetry: demo.provision.failed + demo.runtime.tick_failed log events. Tests: test_demo_legacy.py(11), test_demo_contract.py (cross-surface Plan/Observe/Govern non-empty + referential coherence + coverage-guard partition), test_demo_integration.py (rollback, cleanup, cache coherence, repeated-create, demo_enabled flag, ZERO-network-egress capstone via deny_network fixture + direct service), test_demo_performance.py (provisioning ~187 stmts/6.7s within 500-stmt/45s budget — no bulk-write needed). Docs: new website/docs/use/demo-workspace.md (synthetic vs executable vs preview-only vs unavailable), corrected user-guide note, README. OpenAPI + frontend types regenerated (additive). **FULL BACKEND SUITE: 1323 passed, 0 failures.** Frontend build green. Browser E2E deferred to new child bead (no Playwright harness/full-stack compose in this env; logic covered at vitest/integration level)."}}
{"id":"int-8118b5eb","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T00:01:18.08177652Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2d3d","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Anchored the tolerant plan-diff path to the OLD payload's snapshot_version. _field_changes_between gains old_is_current_version (threaded compute_plan_diff_entries -> _diff_set -> _field_changes_between, computed as old_payload.snapshot_version == PLAN_SNAPSHOT_VERSION). Old payload current-version => a missing change key surfaces as a genuine diff (catches a future conditionally-omitting serializer added to _EVENT/_VARIABLE_CHANGE_KEYS) instead of silent drop; old payload pre-v2 => backward tolerance preserved. Surfacing chosen over a hard assertion so prod never crashes. Tests: current-version base missing key surfaces diff; v1 base missing key still tolerated. test_plan_revisions 8 + test_plan_branches 59 passed; ruff clean."}}
{"id":"int-1c17b399","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T00:02:30.013633235Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-4qfr","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Fact-table preview no longer drops saved manual identifier picks. Root cause: FactTableForm seeded identifierCandidates (the 'previous backend suggestion set') from saved identifier_columns, conflating manual picks with prior suggestions, so the first preview replaced them with only the fresh stricter count_distinct candidates. Fix (no API change): seed identifierCandidates=[] so every saved identifier_column is classified as a manual pick; the existing merge then computes selection = new candidates UNION saved picks (preview ADDs suggestions, never DROPs a saved pick). In-session manual add/remove still persists. Test rewritten: saved paid/android remain checked after a preview that omits them + new country added; manual removal persists on re-preview. vitest 5/5, lint 0, build green."}}
{"id":"int-e2c21e49","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T00:04:17.104163272Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-0s3d","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Collect watcher no longer misbinds after in-page metric navigation. useMetricCollectionWatcher stored only metricId and exposed a raw isWatching bool; MonitoringDetailPage's onSettled invalidated monitoringMetrics with the live render-closure scope/scopeId, and the route has no key so an :id-only nav (A->B) doesn't remount -> B showed a Collecting spinner and A's completion invalidated B's scope. Fix (hook, not a route key which would reset page state): watch(metricId, name, context?) captures caller ids at collect-start into WatchTarget and settle threads them back via onSettled(metricId, status, context); added watchingMetricId so the spinner keys to the specific watched metric (isCollecting = collectMut.isPending || watchingMetricId===scopeId). Page invalidates monitoringMetrics from captured context.scope/scopeId; metricDefinition invalidation unchanged. Other consumer MetricsCatalog unaffected (context optional, isWatching retained). Tests: mid-watch nav doesn't show B collecting; A's completion invalidates ('metric','A') not B. vitest 7 + MonitoringDetailPage 27 (39 total incl. FactTableForm), lint 0, build green."}}
{"id":"int-d3c53f38","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T00:07:28.504633206Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-gf2l","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Sidebar monitoring_signal_count now applies the same incident dedup as AnomaliesPage, so an incident tripping both project_total and event_type on the same (scan_config_id, bucket, direction) counts once on both surfaces. Extracted the rule into shared duck-typed helpers incident_parent_keys(signals) + is_incident_child(signal, parent_keys) in metrics_insights_service.py; _deduplicate_into_incidents rewritten to use them. project_service._populate_monitoring_signals now collects active ProjectLatestSignals, computes parent_keys, and skips incident children before incrementing the count/latest_signal. metric-scope signals (NULL scan_config_id) never match a parent and pass through; batched, no N+1; scan_config_id is project-unique so parent keys never collapse across projects. Test test_signal_count_parity: Scan A (project_total+event_type same key -> 1) + Scan B (unparented event_type -> 1) => count 2 not 3, and summary count == page get_active_signals count. ruff clean; parity + test_projects (21) + test_metrics_api (42) + test_metric_series_api (13) green."}}
{"id":"int-dc4fb784","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T09:38:02.848092589Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.12","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Demo alerting is now zero-egress at three layers.\n\nWorker (the authoritative chokepoint, since scan dispatch / manual retry / stale-pending re-dispatch all funnel through it): send_alert_delivery refuses any non-demo_sink destination on an is_demo project, before rendering — so the AI explanation round-trip cannot fire either. The AI explanation is additionally skipped for demo projects.\n\nAPI: create_destination rejects every external type on a demo project (mirror of the existing demo_sink-only-on-demo rule); update_destination refuses to enable or credential the seeded disabled-Slack example; create_rule/update_rule refuse to arm ai_explanation_enabled on a demo rule rather than silently ignoring it.\n\nFrontend: the Alerting tab reads project.is_demo and, on a demo, replaces the add-channel buttons with an explanation instead of walking the user into a 422.\n\nTests: test_demo_project_never_delivers_to_an_external_destination seeds a demo project with a REAL encrypted, validation-passing Slack webhook and asserts the network tripwire records zero attempts — verified to fail without the guard (it opened a socket to hooks.slack.com), so it genuinely pins the bug. Plus API-level rejection tests and two frontend tests. Backend 87 passed (demo sink + alerting + ai), frontend 6 passed, ruff/mypy/tsc/eslint clean."}}
{"id":"int-aae3ddd8","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T10:46:02.312399917Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.13","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Reset is now atomic. project_service.purge_project_rows() drops the project + its owned synthetic warehouse WITHOUT committing (and flushes, so the DELETE precedes the re-INSERT under the same unique slug); reset_demo_project() calls it, seeds the replacement in place, and commits once at the end. Any failure rolls the whole thing back, so the original demo survives untouched and no hidden failed shell is left behind. Re-seeding under the SAME slug is deliberate: the seed derives the synthetic warehouse name (demo_data_source_name) and the search documents from the slug, so a seed-elsewhere-then-swap design would bake a temporary slug into the content.\n\nRegression test test_failed_reset_leaves_the_existing_demo_untouched injects a seed failure into reset and asserts the demo is still there, still ready, still populated, with no second demo row. Verified RED against the old behaviour: GET /projects/{slug} returned 404 — the demo really was destroyed. 15 passed (lifecycle + integration), ruff/mypy clean."}}
{"id":"int-178e8d2a","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T10:48:49.592931106Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.14","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"DemoBanner's reset now cleans up after the re-seed instead of only invalidating queries. On success it (1) clears the branch selection via useBranchContext().setBranchId(null), which also drops the tripl-branch:{slug} localStorage key — a stale branch id made every branch-aware query fail with 'Branch not found'; (2) navigates to /p/{slug}/overview, because the banner is mounted on every surface and a reset fired from a metric/event/scan detail page left the URL on a now-deleted id; (3) uses queryClient.removeQueries() rather than invalidateQueries(), since every cached row describes a deleted entity. Delete also clears the branch selection so no key is left pointing into a removed project.\n\nThe test harness now wraps the banner in a real BranchProvider (as the Layout does), so the branch clearing is actually exercised — previously useBranchContext fell back to its no-op default and nothing would have been asserted. New test: reset from /p/demo-1/metrics/metric-99 lands on /p/demo-1/overview and leaves no stored branch. 6 passed, tsc/eslint clean."}}
{"id":"int-26863002","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T10:59:07.809332102Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.15","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"The provisioning dialog can no longer trap the user.\n\nRequest: api.post gained an optional AbortSignal and projectsApi.createDemo passes one through. useDemoProvisioning arms an AbortController with a 90s timeout (DEMO_PROVISION_TIMEOUT_MS, overridable via options.timeoutMs so tests need no fake clock) per attempt, clears the timer on settle, and aborts on unmount.\n\nDialog: it is now abandonable rather than un-dismissable while pending — Escape, the close (X) button, an outside click and a real Cancel button in the footer all abort the in-flight request. A user-initiated cancel returns the controller to idle (dialog closes) instead of surfacing the error the abort produces, which an aborted fetch would otherwise become (ApiError 408).\n\nHonesty fix found while doing this: the error copy promised 'Nothing was left behind — the partial demo was rolled back.' That is a lie on a timeout, because the abort only stops OUR request while the server keeps seeding. The hook exposes timedOut and the dialog then says the demo may still be finishing on the server and to check the projects list before creating another.\n\nTests: the old 'is not dismissible while a create is in flight' case encoded the bug and was replaced. New: cancel aborts the signal and lands on idle; a stalled create is aborted once the timeout elapses and reports timedOut; the dialog does not claim a rollback on a timeout. 31 demo tests + ProjectsPage pass, tsc/eslint clean."}}
{"id":"int-dad24eda","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T11:05:56.793678047Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.16","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"The kill switch now actually works, and actually reaches the container.\n\nBypass: POST /projects/demo/{slug}/reset re-provisions a demo from scratch but never called _require_demo_enabled(), so with DEMO_ENABLED=false a full re-seed was still one click away. Reset now calls it. Demo DELETE deliberately stays ungated so a workspace can never be stuck with a demo it cannot remove; the 403 detail is now 'Demo provisioning is disabled' rather than 'Demo creation is disabled', since it covers both paths.\n\nPlumbing: DEMO_ENABLED and DEMO_RUNTIME_ENABLED were absent from compose.yaml (x-app-environment, inherited by api/migrate/worker/beat), compose.dev.yaml (x-backend-environment) and .env.example — so a value set in the compose .env never reached the container and the documented switch was inoperative in Compose. All three now carry both vars, defaulting to true so current behaviour is unchanged.\n\nTest test_kill_switch_gates_reset_as_well_as_create: with demo_enabled=False, create AND reset return 403 while delete still returns 204. 18 passed (lifecycle + rbac), ruff clean."}}
{"id":"int-cff44991","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T11:13:31.762293878Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.17","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"The banner now reports real freshness.\n\nRoot cause: demo_seeded_at is floored to the hour ON PURPOSE — the runtime tick anchors its bucket-index grid to it (demo_runtime.py: 'anchored to demo_seeded_at (immutable)'), so it cannot be changed to a wall-clock stamp. The banner was using it as a freshness signal anyway, so a demo seeded at 10:59 read 'refreshed 59m ago' the instant it appeared, and runtime ticks never moved it.\n\nFix: demo_last_tick_at (the column already existed; the API simply never exposed it) is now on ProjectResponse and the frontend Project type, with openapi.json + api.gen.ts regenerated via make sync-types. The banner reads 'updated {relative(demo_last_tick_at)}' and falls back to 'freshly seeded' before the first tick, rather than inventing a refresh time. Both timestamps carry comments explaining which is which, so the next reader doesn't repeat the mistake.\n\nDeliberately NOT exposing active/paused: _is_paused() keys off demo_last_accessed_at, and project_service bumps that on every GET of the project. Opening the page that renders the banner therefore un-pauses the demo, so a 'paused' badge could never actually be seen there — it would be dead UI.\n\nTests: API exposes demo_last_tick_at (null until first tick); banner shows 'freshly seeded' with no tick and 'updated …' with one. The tick writing the column was already covered (test_demo_runtime.py:285). 10 backend + 8 banner tests pass, ruff/tsc clean."}}
{"id":"int-eed32cd9","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T11:16:17.998432937Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.20","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"The demo's local sink is visible again. ProjectAlertingTab grouped destinations by the six user-selectable channels only, and demo_sink is deliberately not one of them (nobody can add it), so it fell straight through the grouping and its DestinationCard never rendered. The effect on a demo: the Destinations panel showed ONLY the permanently-disabled Slack example, while the sink that actually receives the seeded deliveries was invisible — yet its rules still appeared under Routing rules, so the panel read as self-contradictory.\n\nFix: local sinks get their own 'Local sink' group, rendered above the channel groups, with no delete affordance (the sink belongs to the demo scenario and owns its seeded rules/deliveries; Reset re-creates it). DestinationCard now also badges any is_local destination 'local · nothing is sent', so the zero-egress promise is legible on the card itself rather than only in the banner.\n\nFound while fixing tripl-2su6.12; predates it. Test asserts the sink card, its group heading and the badge all render on a demo. 7 tab tests pass, tsc/eslint clean."}}
{"id":"int-44ef2530","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T11:17:59.822543758Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2gtk","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"summarizeScanChanges labelled time-series ROWS as 'metrics', so an ordinary scan read '+2000 metrics' — as though it had just defined two thousand metric definitions. It sums event_metrics + type_metrics + breakdown_event_metrics + breakdown_type_metrics, which are collected points. Renamed to 'metric point'/'metric points'; docstring and the test assertion updated with a comment recording what the number actually counts. 17 tests pass."}}
{"id":"int-3d53a4da","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T11:24:09.395694517Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-htvg","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Two distinct misbindings, both from reading route state at settle-time instead of capturing it at collect-time.\n\n1) Route race: collectMut.onSuccess re-read scopeId/scope from the render closure. react-query refreshes an observer's options every render, so firing a collect for metric A and navigating to B before the POST resolved made onSuccess attach the watcher to B. The target now travels WITH the mutation (mutationFn takes a CollectTarget; onSuccess receives it back as the variables arg), so nothing downstream re-reads the route.\n\n2) Cross-project poll: the watch target never stored the originating slug — useMetricCollectionWatcher took slug as a hook argument and used the LIVE value in its queryKey/queryFn, so moving to another project mid-watch repointed the poll at project-B/metric-A, an id that does not exist there. slug is now part of the watch request (watch({slug, metricId, displayName, context})) and the hook's slug parameter is gone, so the poll follows the collect it started. Same for the settle-time invalidation in MonitoringDetailPage, which also used the live slug.\n\nAlso fixed while there: isCollecting was , which is mutation-global — navigating to B while A's POST was in flight rendered B as collecting. Now keyed to collectMut.variables?.scopeId.\n\nBoth call sites updated (MonitoringDetailPage, MetricsCatalog). New test asserts the poll never asks project-b for metric A and that the settle invalidates project-a. 109 tests pass across monitoring/metrics/hooks, tsc/eslint clean."}}
{"id":"int-472c7875","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T11:30:44.849422533Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.19","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"The building blocks are real deep links now.\n\nTwo problems, not one. (a) Fact, SQL and Event composition all pointed at a bare /p/{slug}/metrics because the catalog kept its kind filter in component state — there was nothing to link to. The filter now lives in the URL (?kind=), so each block opens the catalog already narrowed, and the filter is shareable/back-button-able as a side effect. Unknown values fall back to no filter rather than querying a bogus kind.\n\n(b) The bigger one: \"Event volume\" is not a metric kind at all. The backend MetricKind enum has exactly three members (fact, sql, event_composition); event volume is the per-event series a scan collects. So that block was not merely under-specific, it pointed at a page that does not contain the thing it describes. It now links to the Events catalog, where the per-event volume actually lives. The docstring claiming \"the four metric kinds\" (and the acceptance criterion it quoted) is corrected in place.\n\nTwo existing tests asserted the buggy behaviour — tourSteps.test.ts expected all four hrefs to equal /p/acme/metrics, and ProductTour.test.tsx looped over the four kinds asserting the same — both rewritten. New assertions: no two blocks share a destination; the catalog calls the API with kind=fact when opened via ?kind=fact; an unknown kind is ignored. 106 tests pass across demo + metrics, tsc/eslint clean."}}
{"id":"int-be79449c","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T11:33:58.899008542Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.18","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"The tour is now followable. The contradiction at its heart: every step deep-links to a REAL surface, so following the tour necessarily closes the dialog — and close() reset the index to 0. Going to step 1s surface and reopening put you back on step 1, forever. It was a stepper that could not be stepped through.\n\nNow: opening a steps surface ADVANCES the tour (visiting is progress, not abandonment) and the position is persisted per project under tripl-tour:{slug}; a plain dismissal (Escape, X, a footer-index link) keeps your place without advancing; Finish — or opening the last steps surface — resets to 0, so a completed tour starts fresh. Out-of-range or unparseable stored values fall back to step 0.\n\nTests: advancing + resuming across a remount, dismissal preserving position, finish resetting, and an out-of-range stored step being ignored. 8 tests pass, tsc/eslint clean.\n\nNOT done (filed separately): the in-page coached scenario — run a scan, watch it land, then collect a metric — would need coach marks on the surfaces themselves, not just a launcher dialog."}}
{"id":"int-955b64b2","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T13:40:00.568832386Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.21.1","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Pure model landed: scenarioModel.ts (reducer + 4 steps + v1 persistence under tripl-demo-scenario:{slug}) and 34 vitest cases covering the happy chain, every regression (scan failed/cancelled/stale, collect error, watch timeout on both watches), artifact binding (newest job wins on double-run; wandering onto another metric's chart does not finish), dismiss/restart inertness, and clamp-on-read for corrupt/v999/unknown-step/malformed-artifact payloads. tsc + eslint clean."}}
{"id":"int-f530c42b","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T13:45:45.890119012Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.21.2","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"DemoScenarioProvider + demoScenarioContext landed and mounted in Layout (inside ProjectEventStreamProvider). Silent artifact polls: scansApi.getJob by the job id the user's run returned (completed -> collect-metric; failed/cancelled -> regress; 404 -> stale, i.e. demo reset) and metricsCatalogApi.get on last_collection_status (success -> see-chart; error/404 -> collect-failed); 5-min timeout on both. Chart step completes at render (the collect can settle while already on the chart). Two contexts (state/actions) with inert defaults -> non-demo pages need no conditionals and never persist. 16 vitest: advance/regress/stale/double-run-newest-wins/reload-resume/chart-completion/wrong-metric/non-demo/seeding/dismiss-survives-remount/restart/mute/no-idle-polling. tsc + eslint clean; Layout + App tests green."}}
{"id":"int-75b21c96","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T13:53:44.597406299Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.21.3","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"DemoScenarioStrip landed, mounted in Layout under DemoBanner (same is_demo gate). Active: 4 progress segments, Dot pulse while a user-started artifact is watched, step title + 'Step N of 4' + instruction in an aria-live region, CTA Link from buildScenarioSteps, hint copy as role=status, Dismiss. Completed: success copy + Restart. Renders null for dismissed/seeding/non-demo (inert context can never read 'completed'). 15 vitest. NOTE: the completed strip has no Dismiss because the model only accepts dismiss while active — a finished scenario therefore sits on every surface until Restart. Fixing in .21.6 (allow dismiss from completed)."}}
{"id":"int-40386083","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T13:53:46.994588546Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.21.4","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"ScenarioCoachMark landed: <ScenarioCoachMark step when? side? align?>{action}</ScenarioCoachMark>. True early return (no Popover in the DOM) unless the scenario is active, unmuted, when!==false and this is the active step — so non-demo pages render byte-identically. Radix PopoverAnchor (asChild when children is a single element) + non-modal PopoverContent role=note showing 'Step N of M' (derived from the chain) + the step instruction + 'Hide hints' (muteHints: quiets marks for the session, scenario keeps running). Focus never leaves the action (onOpen/onCloseAutoFocus prevented, no trap); open with no onOpenChange so Escape/outside-click cannot silence coaching. 7 vitest. tsc + eslint clean."}}
{"id":"int-91f49389","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T14:08:01.265892912Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.21.5","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Wired: notifyScanRunStarted(job) in the three scansApi.run onSuccess sites (ScansTab runAgain, ScanConfigDetailView runMut, ScanDetail retryMut — ScanJob carries scan_config_id, so the returned job is the whole binding) and notifyMetricCollectStarted in both collect sites (MetricsCatalog row menu, MonitoringDetailPage). Coach marks: run-scan on ScanConfigDetailView 'Run now'; watch-scan on the ONE feed row whose job.id === the watched artifact (ScansTab + ScanDetail, via useScenarioArtifacts) so the demo tick's own jobs are never marked; collect-metric on the first visible catalog row's menu + MonitoringDetailPage 'Collect now'; see-chart on the tracked metric's catalog row (NOT the chart — the provider completes that step on arrival, so a mark there would never be read). No run-scan mark inside ScanDetail: it renders as ScanConfigDetailView's tab, which already marks Run now. Non-demo pages are unchanged (inert actions + early-return mark). 12 new tests across MetricsCatalog/MonitoringDetailPage/ScanConfigDetailView/ScanDetail/ScansTab."}}
{"id":"int-39340aa8","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T14:08:03.31597322Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.21.6","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Entry points: 'Run the scenario' (DemoWelcomePanel) and 'Try it hands-on' (ProductTour) — both restart() + navigate to the first step's CTA, both gated on a new context flag 'available' (a ready demo exists) so they never appear on a real project or in a bare unit render. Tour stepper and tripl-tour:{slug} untouched. Hardening: scenarioReducer now accepts dismiss from 'completed' (the success strip was permanent chrome — no dismiss control could exist) and the strip's completed state gained a Dismiss; .pulse-dot got a prefers-reduced-motion guard in index.css (benefits every Dot pulse). Rapid double-run (newest job wins), deleted-metric 404 and demo-reset 404 were already covered by the model/provider suites. 8 new tests (scenarioEntryPoints.test.tsx + model/strip cases)."}}
{"id":"int-82afda23","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-12T14:08:58.796123496Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-2su6.21","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Shipped as .21.1-.21.6 on feat/demo-scenario-coaching. The tour showed the surfaces; the scenario now makes something happen on them: run a scan -> watch it land -> collect a metric -> see the chart move, coached in-page.\n\nLoad-bearing decision: the demo's runtime tick (.7) manufactures real scan jobs and real collections all day, so no step is ever detected as 'a completed job exists'. Progress binds to the artifact the user's own action produced (the ScanJob their run returned, the metric they collected) and lands only when that specific artifact settles; both ids persist, so a reload mid-scan resumes the watch. The SSE contract (.8) is untouched — it hands components no payloads, so the scenario polls its own artifacts, silently (the surfaces already toast).\n\nSurfaces: a persistent strip beside the demo banner (step, progress, CTA, pulse while watching, regression hints, dismiss/restart) plus anchored coach marks on the button that performs the active step. Pages stay dumb — they report actions and wrap an element; the mark early-returns, so a non-demo project renders exactly the DOM it always did. Ways in: 'Run the scenario' (welcome panel) and 'Try it hands-on' (tour). Ways out: dismiss at any point, including after finishing.\n\n117 demo tests + 12 surface tests; full frontend suite 799 green, tsc/eslint clean, build ok."}}
