{"id":"int-cbed0756","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-13T07:23:19.617251226Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-l2so","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"in_progress","reason":"Shipped tests/conformance/test_pipeline_conformance.py (Gate 4): the metrics pipeline now EXECUTES against real PostgreSQL + ClickHouse and ANALYZES against the ZetaSQL emulator for BigQuery.\n\nCovered end to end, driving the REAL worker entrypoints (run_scan, collect_metrics, collect_metric_definitions, collect_fact_metrics_batch, _recalculate_metric_anomalies) — only _get_sync_session/_build_adapter are patched:\n- scan + event generation off a live warehouse (real analyze_cardinality + generate_events)\n- chunked REPLAY collecting event_metrics, plus a second identical replay proving idempotency\n- fact metrics: single (sum/count/count_distinct), ratio (with a dialect-compiled structured condition), per-dimension breakdowns\n- the divide-by-zero contract: a zero-denominator bucket is ABSENT, never 0/inf\n- batched fact collection asserted VALUE-IDENTICAL to the per-metric path (conditional aggregate == aggregate over a filtered subquery, settled on a real engine)\n- event_composition single + ratio\n- drift: event-scope and metric-scope anomaly recalculation over real warehouse output; a constant series must NOT be flagged\n- PG vs CH compared against EACH OTHER and both against core.bucketing.floor_to_bucket\n\ndataset.py extended (not forked) with PIPELINE_ROWS: a 10-bucket 1h series, ~250 rows, baseline 12 / spike 120 (sized to clear the product default min_expected_count=10 — a smaller spike would have made every drift assertion vacuously green).\n\nThe app DB for this gate is REAL PostgreSQL, not SQLite: SQLite returns naive datetimes and takes the sqlite_insert UPSERT branch, so it proves neither the bucket alignment nor the ON CONFLICT that ships.\n\nBigQuery stays ANALYSIS-ONLY by design (emulator is authoritative on validity, NOT on values — its DATETIME_TRUNC(.., WEEK(MONDAY)) is wrong). Stated in the module docstring so nobody 'strengthens' it into a false pass.\n\nAnti-no-op protections intact: verified TRIPL_CONFORMANCE_REQUIRED=1 turns an unreachable warehouse (and an unreachable app DB) into a hard FAILURE, and the CI JUnit guard passes on 119 collected / 0 skipped.\n\nSuite: 119 passed (was 72). Found one P1 production bug: tripl-ju0d (per_distinct_user crashes on ClickHouse — naive vs aware buckets). Reported, NOT fixed; COMP_PER_USER is held out of the executing runs with an in-place comment until it closes."}}
