{"id":"int-b74123564ad23b19bc41643899d295a4","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-27T08:16:21.267906254Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-jfm3.18","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Fixed on prerelease-2-fixes (6d9a000). Scan config create/update/delete and POST /scans/preview (+ the preview-job read) are owner-only — a scan config is free-text SQL interpolated into SELECT * FROM (...) against a stored warehouse credential, and data sources are already owner-only, so the SQL run against them now carries the same role.\n\nDeliberate carve-out: POST /scans/{id}/run stays editor-level. Running a STORED config executes only SQL an owner already authored and approved, so it grants no new read of the warehouse, and the agent API / MCP server drive it with editor-scoped API keys (mcp-server/src/tripl_mcp/tools/scans.py:27). Gating it to owner would have broken that integration without closing the exfiltration vector. Editors keep every read-only view of scans and their jobs.\n\nVerified: test_rbac.py 11 passed, test_scans.py 38 passed."}}
{"id":"int-79807a86883971dc36ede5bd85d7361d","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-27T16:14:41.03471808Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-jfm3.5","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"RESOLVED on prod 2026-07-27. Verified read-only: destination 'Test' (telegram, enabled) carries rule 'TG dev' (enabled), and GET /projects/windy-ios/alert-deliveries returns 2 deliveries both with status 'sent' (16:02:57Z and 16:03:11Z) plus 1 alert-inbox item. The detect -> decide -> route -> notify loop has now executed end to end on the release deployment with real production signals."}}
{"id":"int-3780fa169c89537ee0c059a30c993001","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-27T16:14:52.384879882Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-jfm3.81","extra":{"field":"priority","new_value":"3","old_value":"2"}}
{"id":"int-c96d78c3ca019ee3c29ac9d42db863be","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-27T21:27:32.024917706Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-jfm3.80","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Fixed on prerelease-3-fixes (PR #70). registration_mode now defaults to 'open'; owners get a real control at Settings -> Instance -> Security & access; AuthPage no longer offers a sign-up form on a closed instance; docs gained a :::danger block stating exactly what an open instance exposes (read AND write). The disabled path and its 403 are untouched — all six pre-existing closed-mode tests pass unmodified. Two type drifts fixed on the way: SecuritySettings was missing registration_mode entirely and /auth/status omitted registration_enabled. The missing half — an owner-initiated invite so the default can go back to disabled — is tripl-jfm3.82."}}
{"id":"int-b717511f9b3173e6d04190a67497722a","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-27T21:27:34.482401496Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-jfm3.19","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Fixed on prerelease-3-fixes (PR #70). One reusable ProjectMutationScope now guards the whole mutating surface via get_editor_user, instead of hand-rolled checks across ~20 routers; all 209 routes were enumerated to confirm no GET uses that gate and every per-project mutation is editor- or owner-gated, so future routes are closed by default. Both demonstrated vectors are closed: another user's demo is unreachable by anyone else ever, and a project created by a different editor is closed. Scope resolves in one column-scoped query so authorization never triggers the lazy=selectin plan hydration of tripl-jfm3.54. Data-source connection metadata is now redacted from non-owners. Residual by design — shared owner-created projects remain editable by any editor — split out as tripl-jfm3.85 (needs a real membership model)."}}
{"id":"int-c2c9f9550217d6bac787bfe8bd790c5d","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-27T21:27:37.246020935Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-jfm3.54","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Fixed on prerelease-3-fixes (PR #70). Measured: get_project_by_slug 671.1ms -> 2.5ms, tracker-config 695ms -> 3.5ms, branches 670ms -> 9.7ms, window metrics 6702.5ms -> 17-48ms. Branch diffs now cost one query instead of a per-branch fan-out. Root cause was lazy='selectin' on the project model hydrating the whole plan on every slug lookup. The regression test asserts SQL shape (emitted SELECT count via a before_cursor_execute listener), not wall clock, so it cannot flake on slow hardware."}}
{"id":"int-dd221740f42ddcb9ba0a0d44b1692295","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-27T21:27:39.755154685Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-jfm3.56","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Fixed on prerelease-3-fixes (PR #70), reproduced and verified end-to-end on the local stand's Postgres. Two independent halves: (1) demo plan field values seeded with the default is_authored=False, so the first scan overwrote the hand-authored ${product_id}/${platform} templates with warehouse literals — now seeded is_authored=True, the same stamp event_service applies when a human types a value; (2) delete_variable_contexts_for_event_type deleted EVERY VariableValue for the scanned event type before re-inserting only what the run re-recorded, and the demo's columns are low-cardinality inside their group so the run detects no variables at all -> all three seeded contexts vanished. It now deletes exactly the keys about to be re-added plus rows whose value this run actually rewrote, matching the merge-don't-replace stance _merge_replay_variable_samples already takes. The tripl-jfm3.57 part in scope (the ${product_id}/${platform} overwrite) is fixed with it; .57's core stays open."}}
{"id":"int-ccfb5f9c93d4ec1b6e5b07e3796ab367","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-27T21:27:42.489318629Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-jfm3.81","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Fixed on prerelease-3-fixes (PR #70). The onboarding checklist no longer marks 'Set up alerting' complete on a bare destination — it requires at least one enabled rule, so a project that routes nothing no longer looks finished. Note the correction already recorded on this issue: the original claim of 'destination with 0 rules, nothing routes' on prod was wrong (GET /alert-destinations/{id}/rules is 405; rules are embedded in the destination payload). Prod's real state was rule 'TG dev' enabled with 2 deliveries sent — the checklist logic was still wrong, which is what this closes."}}
{"id":"int-0bf7692a7887c49d25e8b6e8b8f144c5","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-28T08:00:08.826705627Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-jfm3.83","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Fixed in 1d28034 on prerelease-3-fixes (PR #70). /schema now requires editor, /stats requires owner. Boundaries chosen from actual consumers: /schema is used by the scan form, metric form and fact-table form via useDataSourceSchema (all editor surfaces), so owner-only would have broken authoring for the role that does the authoring; /stats has no consumer at all (dataSourcesApi has no stats method, no page calls it, no MCP tool exposes it). Tests pin both directions so a later tightening cannot silently break the scan form. Verified the router does carry protected_dependencies=[Depends(get_current_user)], so the original finding's wording — any AUTHENTICATED user including viewers — was accurate; it was never unauthenticated. openapi.json unchanged (authorization only)."}}
{"id":"int-55fa6a51d32e3ed1600580e2ac489801","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-28T08:18:35.22120692Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-jfm3.84","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Fixed on prerelease-3-fixes (PR #70). The connection summary is now hidden when the payload comes back redacted, keyed off !ds.host rather than the viewer role so it tracks the API's ground truth. The reported empty username chip and missing password lock did not reproduce — both were already guarded, as were the timeout chip and the recovery block; only the connection line was unguarded. Test added: a redacted source renders no ':0/' while still showing name, type and health."}}
{"id":"int-829aa641ea820c0ed8a096e843770a60","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-28T08:56:49.351169392Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-jfm3.87","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Fixed on prerelease-3-fixes (PR #70) in vite.config.ts: maxWorkers is now declarative and CI-conditional, so plain 'pnpm test' is safe by construction and the cap cannot be dropped by the invocation. Root cause confirmed: pnpm appends flags after vitest's own '--' passthrough separator and cac files them into args['--'] without applying or rejecting them. Verified by sampling process count during a real run (cap in effect where the same class of run previously spawned 6 workers, 714 tests passed). No doc change needed — CONTRIBUTING.md and AGENTS.md never carried the broken invocation; it lived only in agent briefs."}}
{"id":"int-bd0934d0fcf656b63a142201058ce27f","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-28T08:58:36.126606286Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-jfm3.86","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Fixed on prerelease-3-fixes (PR #70). The RBAC section now carries the ProjectMutationScope table, states the shared-project consequence explicitly (any editor can edit the tracking plan; with open registration anyone can become that editor), and records why the permissive row is deliberate so it does not get 'fixed' into strict creator-or-owner. Also corrected a stale claim found while writing it: the table listed POST /scans/{id}/run and event-groups/apply as owner-only, but they are editor-gated (verified in scans.py) — running a stored config executes no new SQL and owner-only would break MCP/agent-API automation. Added the tripl-jfm3.83 data-source rows."}}
{"id":"int-77bf081327414d67c9ebc087e7443568","kind":"field_change","created_at":"2026-07-28T08:58:56.547848821Z","actor":"Vladislav Denisov","issue_id":"tripl-jfm3.79","extra":{"field":"status","new_value":"closed","old_value":"open","reason":"Closed as dispersed — every item now lives in a specific issue, none was dropped.\n\nSECURITY: .19 remainder shipped as ProjectMutationScope (closed), residual split to .85 (deferred by owner decision); data-source connection metadata redacted (closed with .19), and the sibling /schema and /stats hole it exposed is .83 (closed); registration_mode UI + AuthPage shipped with .80 (closed).\n\nPERFORMANCE: .54 closed with measurements (671ms -> 2.5ms etc.), including the branch-diff fan-out and window-metrics items listed here; .73 remains open as its own issue.\n\nCORRECTNESS: .57 core (event_name FieldDefinition rendering the group-rule regex) fixed in 6cadb0c, .57 stays open only for the demo user_id/session_id alignment; .56 residual fixed; ingestion settling is now a real ProjectAnomalySettings field with migration, API and MonitoringTab control; anomaly-detection.md documents the detection latency; DEAD_DAYS aligned at 30; Audit action filter fixed.\n\nOPS (still outstanding, owner actions): re-measure the 'Old events (iOS)' scan after deploy — tracked on .1; exercise alerting end-to-end on prod — .5 was closed after prod showed rule 'TG dev' enabled with 2 deliveries sent; ROTATE vlad@windyapp.co's password, which is still not done and is carried forward in this reason so it is not lost with the umbrella."}}
